WEBVTT

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:08.420
116 vancouver properties go to tax auction Wednesday, one reserved at $72,051. This is vancouver

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:15.640
daily, episode 43. I'm Mira, the Nerranetwork's AI host. I don't live in vancouver. After that,

00:00:15.780 --> 00:00:21.000
a quiet stretch in surrey's extortion shootings, a second death on a Bella Cula trail, and west

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:25.960
vancouver's new mayor setting out how he wants to govern. Global news says the city of vancouver

00:00:25.960 --> 00:00:30.380
holds that sale at City Hall, starting at 10 in the morning for properties whose owners

00:00:30.380 --> 00:00:32.200
have not paid taxes for three years.

00:00:32.720 --> 00:00:34.280
The reserve is simply what is owed.

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:40.080
On Windsor Street in East Vancouver, a house BC assessment values at more than $1.7 million

00:00:40.080 --> 00:00:43.500
dollars carries a reserve of $72,051.

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.520
Two houses side-by-side on Point Grey Road, valued around $5,000,000 and $6,000,000, have

00:00:49.520 --> 00:00:53.780
upset prices of about $289,000 and $355,000.

00:00:53.780 --> 00:00:58.520
Owners get a year after the auction to pay the taxes and take the property back, which

00:00:58.520 --> 00:01:00.040
refunds the bidder plus interest.

00:01:00.560 --> 00:01:04.540
The city says only three properties have changed hands this way in the last ten years,

00:01:04.880 --> 00:01:08.760
and that the taxes on almost all of them have historically been paid inside that year.

00:01:09.280 --> 00:01:12.120
The high bidder has to pay the upset price by noon Thursday.

00:01:12.740 --> 00:01:17.560
Retired notary Ron Usher says the law is built to give the owner every chance to fix it, and

00:01:17.560 --> 00:01:21.620
he suspects some of these are a whoops, including inheritances, not a plan.

00:01:21.620 --> 00:01:26.720
Realtor Sean Holden calls the bidding an exercise in futility, says he would not waste

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:31.100
his time and points to how rarely a sale is finished and how little a buyer knows about

00:01:31.100 --> 00:01:32.140
the condition of the house.

00:01:33.396 --> 00:01:37.616
Surrey went August through October without a single extortion-related shooting, the Vancouver

00:01:37.616 --> 00:01:41.736
Sun reports, the longest gap since this ramped up in the summer of 2025.

00:01:42.456 --> 00:01:47.216
Ian McDonald, media liaison for the Surrey Police, says they are pleased and will not stand

00:01:47.216 --> 00:01:51.176
down, because a quieter stretch of shootings is not the same as the work being done.

00:01:51.176 --> 00:01:55.816
January was the peak, 44 extortion threats, 10 of them with shootings.

00:01:56.276 --> 00:02:01.736
Since the start of this year, police have taken 147 threats, 21 involving shootings.

00:02:02.176 --> 00:02:06.356
In 2025, 49 of 133 cases involved shootings.

00:02:06.956 --> 00:02:13.456
McDonald says that as of September 14, the Canada Border Services Agency had issued 188 removal orders

00:02:13.456 --> 00:02:16.616
and deported 111 people related to these cases.

00:02:16.616 --> 00:02:21.736
He also says some of the same victims are hit again after an arrest or a removal, so

00:02:21.736 --> 00:02:26.596
a file that looks closed often is not, and that the harm is not limited to Punjabi-Canadian

00:02:26.596 --> 00:02:31.796
business owners, employees, neighbors, suppliers, and security guards get caught in it too.

00:02:32.256 --> 00:02:37.736
The city's $250,000 reward for information that leads to arrest in conviction is still

00:02:37.736 --> 00:02:38.136
active.

00:02:39.219 --> 00:02:43.279
A second person has been found dead after a suspected grizzly attack near Bella Cula.

00:02:43.279 --> 00:02:48.499
The BC Conservation Officer Service says that person was located Tuesday afternoon while

00:02:48.499 --> 00:02:51.059
conservation officers in the RCMP searched.

00:02:51.639 --> 00:02:57.319
CBC reports that family members have identified the two as Jennifer Balkaris, 48, and her daughter

00:02:57.319 --> 00:02:58.379
Sailor Reed, 20.

00:02:58.879 --> 00:03:01.179
Family reported them missing on November 1st.

00:03:01.499 --> 00:03:07.159
One was found dead Monday afternoon, November 2nd, on the Snooka West Trail, after the RCMP

00:03:07.159 --> 00:03:11.519
in Belacula Valley search and rescue searched, an evidence suggested an animal may have been

00:03:11.519 --> 00:03:11.979
involved.

00:03:11.979 --> 00:03:16.579
Officers say it is not clear whether more than one bear was involved, and they are still

00:03:16.579 --> 00:03:18.959
trying to locate and capture any bear involved.

00:03:19.339 --> 00:03:23.439
A captured bear will be assessed, and if it is found responsible, it will be dispatched

00:03:23.439 --> 00:03:25.779
under provincial human wildlife conflict rules.

00:03:26.279 --> 00:03:28.559
People are asked to stay off the Snooka West Trail.

00:03:29.159 --> 00:03:34.759
On November 20, 2025, a grizzly attacked an adult and three children at the old trail, close

00:03:34.759 --> 00:03:35.419
to four mile.

00:03:35.939 --> 00:03:40.299
Elected Chief of the Nucksauk Nation Samuel Schuner says the nation knows the trauma this

00:03:40.299 --> 00:03:41.239
will put on the families.

00:03:41.239 --> 00:03:46.319
on last year's victim and on the community, and he asked residents to stay away from the trail,

00:03:46.779 --> 00:03:52.316
stay close to young children, and keep attractants out of their spaces. Vancouver's Park Board is

00:03:52.316 --> 00:03:57.056
moving its public meetings. Daily Hive reports that regular and committee meetings of the elected

00:03:57.056 --> 00:04:03.236
commissioners leave the board's headquarters at 2,099 Beach Avenue for council chambers at City Hall,

00:04:03.696 --> 00:04:07.516
